hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15564","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Khalid, meaning Ibn Abdullah, narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, he said: My uncle Wasi ibn Hibban narrated to me, from Wahb ibn Hudhayfah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is most entitled to his seat, even if he rises from it then returns, so he is most entitled to it."
"15565","Affan narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from his uncle Wasi ibn Hibban, from Wahb ibn Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a man rises from his seat then returns to it, he is most entitled to it, even if he had a need and rose to it then returned, he is most entitled to it."
